  {
   "id": "stock",
   "chapter": "What is a stock? (IPO)",
   "audio": "vo/s2.mp3",
   "audioFrom": 8,
   "from": 409,
   "frames": 720,
   "phrases": [
    {
     "text": "First, what is a stock?",
     "start": 11,
     "end": 81
    },
    {
     "text": "It's a tiny slice of ownership in a company.",
     "start": 81,
     "end": 172
    },
    {
     "text": "When a company wants money to grow,",
     "start": 172,
     "end": 208
    },
    {
     "text": "it can split itself into millions of shares,",
     "start": 208,
     "end": 301
    },
    {
     "text": "and sell some of them to the public.",
     "start": 301,
     "end": 366
    },
    {
     "text": "That first sale is called an IPO,",
     "start": 366,
     "end": 444
    },
    {
     "text": "an initial public offering,",
     "start": 444,
     "end": 479
    },
    {
     "text": "and the cash goes to the company.",
     "start": 479,
     "end": 560
    },
    {
     "text": "After that, investors trade those shares with each other.",
     "start": 560,
     "end": 665
    },
    {
     "text": "That's the stock market.",
     "start": 665,
     "end": 703
    }
   ],
